      "data": {
        "text": "**Considering Secret Management**\n\nOkay, I'm thinking about the implementation details. I've decided to use Google Cloud Secret Manager for handling the API key. Now, the next step is to figure out the best way to integrate it into the Python script to make it secure.\n\n\n**Implementing Secret Retrieval**\n\nI'm now focused on the code. I'm creating `fetch_api_key.py`, which will fetch the API key using Google Cloud Secret Manager. I've decided to use `google.cloud.secretmanager` as the provider. I'm implementing a function that takes the project and secret IDs as input, constructs the secret name, accesses the latest version, and returns the payload.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789818713998,
          "start": 1789818712477
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0b982319d001wC72F9vzPFnatw",
